<title>UK: BASKETBALL-MEN'S EUROLEAGUE RESULTS.</title>
<headline>BASKETBALL-MEN'S EUROLEAGUE RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results from the final round of</p>
<p>group matches in the second preliminary round of the men's</p>
<p>EuroLeague basketball championship on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Group G</p>
<p>In Athens: Panathinaikos (Greece) 75 Pau Orthez (France) 71</p>
<p>(halftime 31-41)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Panathinaikos - Byron Dinkins 15, Michael Koch 13, Marcelo</p>
<p>Nikola 13</p>
<p>Pau Orthez - Fabien Dubos 20, Thiery Gadou 19, Colin Crauder</p>
<p>11</p>
<p>Group G</p>
<p>In Ljubljana:  Ljubljana (Slovenia) 80 Dynamo Moscow</p>
<p>(Russia) 72 (42-41)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Ljubljana - Arriel McDonald 14</p>
<p>Moscow - Oleg Malescenko 15</p>
<p>Attendance: 2,500</p>
<p>Group G</p>
<p>In Villeurbanne: Villeurbanne (France) 83 Sevilla (Spain) 81 (45-46)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Villeurbanne - Delaney Rudd 18, Remy Ripper 12, Brian Howard 10, Jim Bilba 10</p>
<p>Sevilla - Raul Perez 19, Tellis Frank 11, Michael Anderson 10</p>
<p>Attendance: 5,500</p>
